Step 1 — Don't code yet

                The strongest way to model N-Queens is row by row.                
                Why?
                
                Because every valid solution has exactly one queen in every row.                
                So our recursion can represent:
                              row = current row where we need to place a queen

                At each row:
                            choose a column
                                ↓
                            check whether that position is safe
                                ↓
                            place queen
                                ↓
                            recurse to next row
                                ↓
                            remove queen


So the backtracking skeleton becomes:
                                          solve(row)
                                          
                                          for each column:
                                              if position is safe:
                                                  choose
                                                  solve(row + 1)
                                                  undo
